  indexes {
    (ablId, ablAccYear) [pk]
  }

  Note: 'One row per bill. Partitioned by ablAccYear — the FY the bill was RAISED in
— so the primary key is the composite (ablId, ablAccYear) and a bill is
addressed by the PAIR, never by the id alone.

The bill is never carried forward at year end: the same row stays open
across financial years, in the partition of the year it started in. So the
partition says "where it started", not "where the money is" — outstanding
and ageing reads carry no year filter and scan every partition, and
detaching a closed year takes its still-open bills with it. Every reference
into the bill carries the bill\'s own year alongside the id
(AccBillAdjustment.abjBillAccYear, AccVoucher.avDocAccYear, ablParentAccYear
below), which is what makes a settlement in a later year expressible.

ablAllocAmount / ablDiscAmount / ablWriteoffAmount are declared
trigger-maintained from AccBillAdjustment and must never be written from
application code.'
}

